This module reimplements Source Control behavior specified by Visual Studio Code
(Code - OSS) and its built-in Git extension, read at commit
ef5ca45a6e545e4767e0117905ee9d6120b86e11. No VS Code source is copied. Where an
algorithm follows VS Code closely, such as the sorting of a status into merge,
staged and changes groups, the Changes tree's compressed folders and sort
orders, the repository rows, the view's menus and inline actions with their
order and conditions, the selection an action runs on, and discarding changes
with its questions, the trash first and the offer to delete permanently, the
MIT license below covers it.

